  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.0.13\"\n\npackage:\n  name: torchax\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/google/torchax/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 9a88a6d83e01241ff0e6fd55798541d74d4d4b2d76f19c6f0733bbe2042c0de0\n  patches:\n    # Backports of google/torchax#99, #102 and #108 for current PyTorch.\n    - remove-cholesky.patch\n    - pytorch-2.13-compatibility.patch\n    - optional-qr.patch\n    # Approved upstream: https://github.com/google/torchax/pull/110\n    - optional-distributed.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: python -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python =${{ python_min }}\n    - hatchling\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - jax >=0.6.2\n    - numpy\n    - optax\n    - pytorch >=2.8\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      site_packages:\n        - torchax\n  # conda-forge does not publish jaxlib for Windows:\n  # https://github.com/conda-forge/jaxlib-feedstock/issues/161\n  - if: not win\n    then:\n      - script:\n          - python -m pip check\n          - python test_torchax.py\n        requirements:\n          run:\n            - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n            - pip\n            # Select the BLAS provider for CI only.\n            - libblas * *openblas\n        files:\n          recipe:\n            - test_torchax.py\n      - script:\n          - python -m pip check\n          - python test_torchax.py\n        requirements:\n          run:\n            - python\n            - pip\n            - libblas * *openblas\n        files:\n          recipe:\n            - test_torchax.py\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/google/torchax\n  summary: PyTorch frontend for JAX and graph-level interoperability\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  documentation: https://google.github.io/torchax/\n  repository: https://github.com/google/torchax\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - anutosh491\n",
